From: overpressure <overpressure@pico4>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: the unaligned atomic fixup's 128-bit load survives a read-only page

Load128 reads with a store back, and only its load had an exception table entry. On a page that
reads but does not write yet (copy-on-write) the store ends in "Unable to handle kernel access to
user memory outside uaccess routines", and the oops takes the thread with it: a Unity game under
FEX stays in its first load forever. With the entry the fixup reports the fault, the fault handler
resolves it as the store it is and the instruction runs again. Every other store in the file has
its entry.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/unaligned_atomic.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/unaligned_atomic.c
index 28868ad0a3fe..8a31e8b04764 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/unaligned_atomic.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/unaligned_atomic.c
@@ -129,10 +129,11 @@ static struct fault_info Load128(u64 Addr, u128* Result) {
 
   uaccess_enable_privileged();
   asm volatile("1: ldaxp %[ResultLower], %[ResultUpper], [%[Addr]]\n"
-               "   stlxp %w[Tmp], %[ResultLower], %[ResultUpper], [%[Addr]]\n"
+               "2: stlxp %w[Tmp], %[ResultLower], %[ResultUpper], [%[Addr]]\n"
                "   cbnz %w[Tmp], 1b\n"
-               "2:\n"
-               _ASM_EXTABLE_UACCESS_ERR(1b, 2b, %w[ret])
+               "3:\n"
+               _ASM_EXTABLE_UACCESS_ERR(1b, 3b, %w[ret])
+               _ASM_EXTABLE_UACCESS_ERR(2b, 3b, %w[ret])
                : [Tmp] "=&r"(Tmp), [ResultLower] "=&r"(Lower), [ResultUpper] "=&r"(Upper), [ret] "+r"(ret)
                : [Addr] "r"(Addr)
                : "memory");
